+- `scene`: Describe how the sequence begins, then the progression of events in order, drawing only on the observations. A brief activity needs only a sentence or two. For named subjects (those with a `←` separator in "Objects in Scene"), always use their name — do not replace them with generic terms. For unnamed objects (e.g., "person", "car"), refer to them naturally with articles (e.g., "a person", "the car"). Your description should align with and support the threat level you assign.
+- `title`: A short phrase naming the primary activity. Name an interaction with an object only when it is plainly visible; otherwise name the movement (e.g., "Person walks up the driveway"). For named subjects, always use their name. For unnamed objects, refer to them naturally with articles.
+- `shortSummary`: One natural sentence of at most 20 words, with articles, about the primary activity, shown as a phone notification. Include only what is clearly visible. Leave out the time, date, duration, weather, and lighting, and do not mention the subject leaving.
